## THE WORK (each check: the FAIL first with the clock, your instrument, a control that can fail; predictions to evidence with sha256 BEFORE the run)
- **D1. Delta and hygiene (cheap, first).** FAIL: a path other than the one; a changed line other than the three removed; a product or config byte. `git diff --name-only b9de932b 0c10a4dc` the one file; numstat `20 3`; the 3 removed lines are exactly those named in FACTS and the 20 added lines are the comment, helper, two clock reads and the timeout (control: a planted extra removed line is counted); the other 57 main lines present in order and the first row (main lines 19-27) a byte-equal contiguous block, `.toBeLessThan(1000)`, the loop and `durations[3]` present (your own line-set comparison; control: a planted changed character in the first row). Added lines: ASCII only (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^\+.*[^ -~]'` 0; control: a planted raw byte 1), no tab, CR or bidi (planted U+202E built at run time fires), **no skipped, focused, retried, soft, timer-driven or console row** (the shapes at least `it.skip`, `.only`, `.todo`, `skipIf`, `runIf`, `retry`, `xit`, `test.fails`, `expect.soft`, `console.`, `setTimeout`, `vi.useFakeTimers`, `new RegExp(`; control: planted; English uses of the word "only" in a comment are Notes), no person, client or sample-client name (a run-time list, never written), no card slug, `PCOMP-`, `#<n>`, `B<digits>` in the added lines or the message. Identity: author and committer emails end `@users.noreply.github.com`, `localdomain` 0 (control `dc16530a...` reads 1), the tuple equals main's latest 8 (domain and "pair equal y" only); trailer exactly 1 (control 0) and it reads `Claude Sonnet 5.5`. gitleaks `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks`: a random `ghp_`-shaped canary written at run time into scratch rc 1 FIRST, then `b9de932b..0c10a4dc` rc 0, chained with `&&`.
- **D2. THE FACTOR OF TWO (first heavy job; THING 2).** FAIL: the committed file's hog median not reproduced by you within the spread you print, OR a variant that reproduces 629-822 ms that you cannot name. Build `pc-b1101-node:head` (`docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f '<tree>/docker/Dockerfile' --target ci -t pc-b1101-node:head '<tree>'`; `RUN npm ci --ignore-scripts` CACHED); record `node --version` (builder: v22.23.2), npm, vitest (builder: 5.0.0), `typeof process.threadCpuUsage` in the image. **Write predictions first, with sha256:** H1 (the swap did not take: a wall clock) predicts medians 600-900 ms and row duration / (8 x median) about 1.0; H2 (`process.cpuUsage()`, the process total) predicts medians between the thread figure and the wall figure, larger than the thread figure by the GC helpers' share, ratio below 2.4 and above 1.0; the committed bytes predict 250-340 ms and a ratio about 2.4-2.7. Then in the hog, ONE batch container per rep, interleaved variants, **10 reps each** (the heavy-job budget below), each variant printed with its file hash: **C** the committed file; **W** the committed file with the two clock reads set back to `performance.now()` (the old clock, with the 60,000 ms timeout); **P** the committed file with `threadMs` forced to `process.cpuUsage()` (the fallback path, and also H2); **S** a rebuild of the builder's first-stop description ("`performance.now()` replaced by `process.threadCpuUsage()`", which you must write yourself as a text replace and may not read from its scratch copy: the replacement as an object subtraction would give NaN, so say what you did). Print per variant: median min/median/max, the row duration, the ratio, and the clock probe (e) in the same container. **The answer is one of: reproduced (name the variant), explained (name the mechanism with the probe's numbers), or UNEXPLAINED.** Grade: an unexplained factor of two beside the clock the lane stands on is class (a), **Major** if C cannot be reproduced in your cells or if you cannot rule out that the committed file's median depends on how the file is run; if C reproduces and S/W/P explain the scratch figure, the finding is a Note with the mechanism. Also print the committed-bytes range from YOUR cells against the file comment's "250-304 ms" (class (e), Minor) and the message's "262-333 ms".
- **D3. Green at head, quiet and hog, stable.** In `pc-b1101-node:head` through your runner: main file quiet x3 (expected green; the PERF line prints, else STOP) and under the hog x10 (builder: 8 of 10 red by "Test timed out in 5000ms"; print your count and the messages); head file quiet x3, **under the hog x10 with 0 red by any message** (your cells, not the builder's), the row alone once (`-t`, with the JSON reader asserting passed 1 and a title match; a solo run with 0 matches is an instrument failure), one `--sequence.shuffle` seed once; per cell the verdict, row duration, PERF median and 7 durations, `load1` before and after, the probe's CPU-seconds in 5 s and `nr_throttled`. **INVALID (rerun, never averaged): host load1 >= 9 at the cell start, or the probe below 9 CPU-s in 5 s with the loops.** If load never allows 10 valid hog cells, report the valid count and say the verdict is conditional. Report the worst row duration (builder: 7,083 ms; the timeout 60,000 ms = 8.5 x it, and a quarter of it is 15,000 ms: ADDENDUM-1 line 10 says re-derive only if a new worst exceeds that; P4's rows were 11.7 and 15.3 s, print yours). The thin margin: head max against 1000 (builder 333.0 ms).
