## GRADING (binding; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (D1).** A second path, a product or config byte = **Blocker** (hand-up if security-shaped); a changed line other than the three removed, or a changed bound, loop, warm-up, median index, fixture or title = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, secret or card slug = **Blocker**; non-ASCII or a skip/focus/retry/timer/console row in the added lines = **Major**; `localdomain` = **Major**; a false commit sentence = **Minor** (corrected in `squash-body.txt`); a Jira key or work number in an added line = **Minor**.
- **G-2 the clock (D2, D4, D5).** The factor of two unexplained = **Major, class (a)**; explained = **Note** with the mechanism; the committed file red in any valid hog cell or flaky = **Major, class (d)**; P1/P2 not red by the assertion = **Major** (the row cannot fail); P4 red = STOP; a plausible slowdown the old row caught, the new row misses and the cost sentence does not name = **Major, class (b)**, else **Minor** (wording); fallback max at or over the bound = **Major, class (c)**, 800-1000 ms = **Minor**; a comment or message number the runs do not back = **Minor, class (e)**, **Major** only if it is about the detection claim.
- **G-3 the reading (THING 1).** Not graded as a code defect: the gate reports, with measurements, whether the clock choice is defensible against the title, the header, the ticket's fix shape and the prior art, and what the alternatives would have cost; a finding only for a false or missing sentence about it. The decision is the coordinator's and, if it must be ruled, the product owner's on a card.
- **G-4 the rows and the cost (D3, D6, D7).** A hog or quiet cell red by any message at head (valid cells) = **Major, class (d)**; lint or prettier rc non-zero on the file = **Major**; no tsc covering `packages/engine/test` = **Note** (pre-existing); the `s47-crf2` row red under the hog = **Note** for Tuesday (outside the lane).
- **G-5 merge and CodeQL (D8).** A conflict, a merge tree that differs from the expected tree, or a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; an open alert = **Blocker** and STOP; CodeQL NOT SCANNED (no PR) = a **Condition**. **Always Note:** the dependabot banner, the builder's `/tmp/x` and other conduct slips (relayed).
- **G-6 verdict (round 1 of 2).** Any Blocker or Major = `NO GO (round 1 of 2)` (fix-shapes in prose; "a second NO GO on this class goes to the product owner on a card"); Minors/Notes only = `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; none above Note = `GO`. Always add ` (conditional: NO PR; CodeQL NOT SCANNED)` and any other unrun required check.

## LOAD (binding)
8 cores shared (load1 14.82 at 06:12; other projects' panes live; J41 may hold the lock). Heavy = `docker build`, any container run, any vitest run, the hog batches. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent: say so), recorded beside each result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (reading, writing your programs). **One heavy job at a time, behind your seat lock `.tools/b1101/lock` AND the project lock `.tools/composer-heavy.lock`; you WAIT on another seat's holder.** A MOVING heartbeat to `.tools/b1101/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a wait loop never uses `pgrep -f`/`ps | grep` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets `/dev/null` or its input. **Budget (write it at Step 0; keep the real count in `starts.log`):** build 1; clock probe 1; D2 batches 10 (each runs C, W, P, S in sequence behind one build and one hog); D3 main-hog 10 cells may share the D2 batches (add M to the batch list: say so) plus quiet 3, row alone 1, shuffle 1; D4 plants P0-P4 about 5 containers, P5-P7 3, the unedited-main contrasts 2; D5 shares D2; D6 crf2 file 1; D7 lint/format/tsc 1, the chain 1 (optional); plants and controls 4. About 30 starts; if your count passes 45, say so. A hog cell takes about 7-35 s plus the build (about 3 minutes per container): batch variants so the build is paid once.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh, no HTTP to any hosted host or the demo site. Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` a container you did not create. Network: your one in-clone fetch, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`; no POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE, no `gh pr create`, no re-run; **no Jira call** (the ticket text above is your data). Git in `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`), worktree add ONLY `.tools/wt-b1101-{main,head,mut}` detached (assert `HEAD` and `HEAD^{tree}`: main `bd4a0516...`, head `1e88d781...`); clone/fetch/merge-tree/read-tree/write-tree/archive only in `.tools/b1101/repo` (a plain `git clone --no-hardlinks`, never `--shared`; push URL `DISABLED-no-push`). **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW (the unit step binds the SOW text read-only and never opens it), `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` beyond that mount, or `inbound/`. No decision-queue, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` beyond the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (quarantine to `.tools/b1101/quarantine/`; do not type `rm`). **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (space and `!`); `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (a separator line is `echo ----`); chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script (zsh is the interactive shell: no unquoted list variable, and a bang inside double quotes is history-expanded: build bang text in files); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I -B`; write programs with the Write tool and read them back. Plants live ONLY in `wt-b1101-mut`, a container's own layer and scratch. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"), no card slug. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR WORK section in STATUS (what you read of the builder lane; what you reuse: plumbing only, and the hog recipe as DATA; a READY-style claim without it is returned); Jira writes none; nothing to any human; never delete. **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections, plants restored with proof, processes and containers stopped, both locks released by move, last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?`.

